Package: cudaverseCUDA
Title: Native CUDA Backend Extension for Cudaverse
Version: 0.4.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Yaoxiang", "Li", email = "liyaoxiang@outlook.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Provides an optional lightweight native CUDA backend for the
    'cudaverse' package. The extension dynamically discovers the NVIDIA CUDA
    Driver, cuBLAS, and cuSOLVER libraries at runtime and implements device
    diagnostics, allocation, host-device transfer, dense and sparse storage,
    reductions, matrix multiplication, normalization, singular-value
    decomposition, principal-component analysis, exact distances, and stable
    nearest-neighbour selection without linking to 'LibTorch' or requiring a
    CUDA Toolkit during package installation.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
URL: https://github.com/cudaverse/cudaverseCUDA
BugReports: https://github.com/cudaverse/cudaverseCUDA/issues
Encoding: UTF-8
Language: en-US
SystemRequirements: NVIDIA CUDA driver; NVIDIA cuBLAS 12 at runtime for matrix multiplication; NVIDIA cuSOLVER 11 at runtime for SVD and PCA
Imports:
    cudaverse (>= 0.2.0.9000)
Remotes:
    cudaverse/cudaverse@develop/native-cuda
Suggests:
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
NeedsCompilation: yes
